Role: Senior Software Engineer - Java

&nbsp; 

Experience: &nbsp; 4-6 Years. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Location: Rajajinagar, &nbsp; Bangalore&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Job Type: On-site&nbsp; - WFO

&nbsp; 

Job Summary: &nbsp; 

We are&nbsp; seeking&nbsp; a highly skilled Microservices Developer with&nbsp; expertise&nbsp; in Java, Spring Boot, MongoDB, MySQL, Redis, and RabbitMQ. The ideal candidate will&nbsp; be responsible for&nbsp; designing, developing, and&nbsp; maintaining&nbsp; scalable microservices architectures while ensuring high performance and reliability. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities: &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

- Develop and maintain microservices-based applications using Java and Spring Boot. &nbsp; 
 - Design and implement RESTful APIs with best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Work with MongoDB and MySQL for data storage, ensuring efficient database design and querying. &nbsp; 
 - Implement caching solutions using Redis to enhance application performance. &nbsp; 
 - Integrate and manage RabbitMQ for efficient message brokering and asynchronous processing. &nbsp; 
 - Write clean, scalable, and well-documented code following best software development practices. &nbsp; 
 - Ensure unit testing and integration testing using frameworks like JUnit, Mockito, etc. &nbsp; 
 - Optimize&nbsp; and debug performance bottlenecks in the system. &nbsp; 
 - Collaborate with DevOps teams to ensure seamless deployment and CI/CD integration. &nbsp; 
 - Work in an Agile environment, &nbsp; participating&nbsp; in sprints, code reviews, and daily standups. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Required Skills & Qualifications: &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

- 4-6&nbsp; years of hands-on experience in Java, Spring Boot, and microservices development. &nbsp; 
 - Strong knowledge of MongoDB and MySQL, including query optimization and indexing. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Redis for caching and performance optimization. &nbsp; 
 - Hands-on experience with RabbitMQ or other message brokers. &nbsp; 
 - Strong understanding of RESTful API design, authentication, and security best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Familiarity with containerization tools (Docker, Kubernetes) is a plus. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with cloud platforms (AWS / Azure / GCP) is a plus. &nbsp; 
 - Strong knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices. &nbsp; 
 - Excellent problem-solving and debugging skills. &nbsp; 
 - Strong communication&nbsp; and collaboration skills. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Apply Here: &nbsp; 

Apply on Linkedin or Send your resume to hr@erelego. com

Company Address: &nbsp; www. erelego. com&nbsp;

About the role
As a Systems Engineer Manager you are the first systems engineering management role. You impact positively the teams you lead, the people you manage and the products you are responsible for whilst helping build the right culture within your domain. You hire, develop, and retain our System Engineers to set them up for success. You build performing teams that consistently deliver quality outcomes, whilst empowering your engineers to own technical decisions. You work effectively with your stakeholders and product teams to ensure the right outcomes are delivered. You play a key role in formulating the technical strategy and roadmap for your area. 
You will be responsible for
Following
our Business Code of Conduct and always acting with integrity and due diligence
and have these specific risk responsibilities: 

I play an active role in
people management and technical leadership. I impact the teams I lead, the
people I manage and the products I am responsible for, whilst having a direct
impact upon the environment and continuous improvement within my domain. I am
responsible for building and developing high performing teams. I take
accountability for the environment that my teams operate within and the
processes and standards that facilitate high quality systems delivery. Ensuring
the right product outcomes through the right technical strategy and trade-offs. 
I build capability by hiring, retaining, and developing the careers of our
engineers, ensuring opportunities for growth, and maintaining a level of
challenge and motivation. 

